    },
    "message": "Finish the queues, resources and population rules in Rust (lanes L1 and L4)\n\nThe kernels stop refusing what a valid Run reaches:\n- _abandon_and_retry for both kinds of queue, with the walk back and the record.\n- Cancelling and interrupting a service read the rows, without the manager's helpers.\n- The driver runs the independent queues' loops itself.\n- A busy departure or exit schedules its retry and suppresses with the rule's text.\n- A suppressed information contact, likewise.\n- First use makes the population state and an absent social namespace.\n- Receipts of every kind, and recent receipts not yet checked go to their contract.\n- A tick's check of the population state calls its kernel.\n- A closed route stops staff trips in Rust.\n- A model with no long-term state makes that step do nothing.\n- The two call-backs after a write are gone: what the admission asks is asked first.\n- handlers.rs calls kernels directly; population's room reads live in overlay.rs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K4QyYRukuCLBerKa4UYj4y",
